---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import FeedbackEmigrationGame from "../../components/FeedbackEmigrationGame.svelte";
import Header from "../../components/Header.svelte";
import { changelog } from "../../js/emegration-changelog";

const VERSION = changelog[0].version;

const ID = "emigration";
const FILES_PATH = `/files/${ID}/v${VERSION}/`;

let printAndPlay = [
  {
    name: "Mini Cards",
    title: `${ID}-game-mini-cards-v${VERSION}.pdf`,
    pages: "8 pages",
  },
  {
    name: "Small Square Cards",
    title: `${ID}-game-small-square-cards-v${VERSION}.pdf`,
    pages: "1 page",
  },
  {
    name: "Medium Chits (optional)",
    title: `${ID}-game-medium-chits-v${VERSION}.pdf`,
    pages: "1 page",
  },
  {
    name: "Small Chits (optional)",
    title: `${ID}-game-small-chits-v${VERSION}.pdf`,
    pages: "1 page",
  },
];
---

<Header client:idle />
<Layout title="Emigration Board Game">
  <main
    class="max-w-screen-md w-full text-left m-auto px-2 pb-8 font-publicSans"
  >
    <div class="my-4">
      <picture>
        <source
          srcset="/files/emigration/Emigration-Game-Logo.webp"
          type="image/webp"
        />
        <source
          srcset="/files/emigration/Emigration-Game-Logo.png"
          type="image/png"
        />
        <img
          src="/files/emigration/Emigration-Game-Logo.png"
          alt="Emigration Game Logo"
        />
      </picture>
      <p class="uppercase tracking-widest text-center">
        A board game about moving abroad
      </p>
      <div
        class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 justify-center items-center mb-4 opacity-50"
      >
        <p>2-6 Players</p>
        <p>20-60 Minutes</p>
        <p>Ages 14+</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p
      class="mt-4 text-4xl uppercase tracking-widest font-bold break-words text-red-500 text-center"
    >
      Prototype
    </p>

    <p class="px-4 py-2 w-fit mx-auto mb-2">
      Version {VERSION} - <a href="/emigration/changelog" class="underline"
        >View Changelog</a
      >
    </p>

    <p class="my-4 text-lg">
      You're moving to another country! Scramble to collect documents, make
      valuable connections, and manage your money as life happens. Then pick a
      border control line and hope the officer lets you in!
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mt-8 mb-4 justify-center items-center">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 justify-center items-start">
        <a
          href="/emigration/emulator"
          class="btn bg-amber-300/70 dark:bg-amber-700/70 hover:bg-amber-200 dark:hover:bg-amber-800"
          ><span>&#9654;</span> Play</a
        >
        <a
          href={FILES_PATH + `${ID}-game-rulebook-v${VERSION}.pdf`}
          download={`${ID}-game-rulebook-v${VERSION}.pdf`}
          class="btn"
          ><svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke-width="1.5"
            stroke="currentColor"
            class="w-6 h-6 flex-none"
          >
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              d="M3 16.5v2.25A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75V16.5M16.5 12L12 16.5m0 0L7.5 12m4.5 4.5V3"
            ></path>
          </svg>
          Rulebook</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="inline-flex flex-col gap-2 my-2 items-start">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-4xl mb-2">Print & Play</h2>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 items-center justify-start">
          {
            printAndPlay.map((item) => (
              <a
                href={FILES_PATH + item.title}
                download={item.title}
                class="btn-sm"
              >
                <svg
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                  fill="none"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  stroke-width="1.5"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  class="w-6 h-6 flex-none"
                >
                  <path
                    stroke-linecap="round"
                    stroke-linejoin="round"
                    d="M3 16.5v2.25A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75V16.5M16.5 12L12 16.5m0 0L7.5 12m4.5 4.5V3"
                  />
                </svg>
                {item.name} - {item.pages}
              </a>
            ))
          }
        </div>

        <div class="inline-flex flex-col gap-2 my-2 text-left">
          <p class="">
            To Print & Play, you'll need a printer and some time to cut out all
            the cards. You'll also need <span class="font-black"
              >One Six-Sided Die</span
            >. If you don't print the optional Small and Medium Chits, you'll
            need Money (about 20 per player) and Assurance (about 10 per
            player); you can use a different game's pieces for those.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="inline-flex flex-col gap-2 my-2 items-start">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-4xl mb-2">Q&A</h2>
        <p class="font-bold">Where can I buy the game?</p>
        <p>
          You can't buy the game yet. But you can test the game by playing it in
          the emulator or by printing the game yourself. Eventually, we'd like
          to make the game available to buy through <a
            href="https://www.thegamecrafter.com/games/emigration"
            target="_blank"
            class="underline">The Game Crafter</a
          >.
        </p>

        <p class="font-bold mt-4">How can I ask a question or give feedback?</p>
        <p>
          Use the feedback form at the bottom of this webpage,
          <a
            href="https://discord.gg/aDV6NY73H2"
            target="_blank"
            class="underline cursor-pointer">join the Discord Server</a
          >, or email feedback@tandagames.com.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="inline-flex flex-col gap-2 my-2 items-start w-full">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-4xl mb-2">Get Notified</h2>
        <p>
          We'll let you know when the game is available and any news regarding
          development.
        </p>
        <form
          target="_blank"
          action="https://formsubmit.co/99157ff313bd346ac1d729cca203b666"
          enctype="multipart/form-data"
          method="POST"
          class="inline-flex flex-wrap items-start justify-start gap-2 text-left max-w-md"
        >
          <input type="hidden" name="version" value={VERSION} />

          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 flex-1">
            <label for="name-or-alias" class="text-sm opacity-70"
              >Your name</label
            >
            <input
              id="name-or-alias"
              type="text"
              name="Your Name"
              placeholder="Your Name"
              class=""
            />
          </div>

          <div class="basis-full"></div>

          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 flex-1">
            <label for="email-address" class="text-sm opacity-70"
              >Your email</label
            >
            <input
              id="email-address"
              type="email"
              name="email"
              placeholder="email@example.com"
              class=""
            />
          </div>

          <div class="basis-full"></div>

          <button type="submit" class="btn">Signup for Updates</button>
        </form>
      </div>

      <div class="inline-flex flex-col gap-2 my-2 items-start">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-4xl mb-2">Elements Needing Analysis</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc ml-8">
          <li>
            <span class="font-bold"
              >Optimal (or suboptimal) Life Card combinations.</span
            > What are the best (or worst) Life Cards to use for different types of
            game dynamics and number of players? (For example, what Life Cards&#8212;when
            used together&#8212;encourage wealth building, cutthroat competition,
            friendly play, or drastic events? Or what Life Card combinations do not
            work well together?)
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-bold">Game-breaking strategies.</span> Are there any
            strategies which always create predictable outcomes or ruin the game for
            other players? (For example, maybe always discarding Documents and Connections
            instead of buying them always gets you more Assurance than not.)
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="my-2">
          If you can help analyze any of these game elements, or have any other
          observations, please share your feedback using the form below, <a
            href="https://discord.gg/aDV6NY73H2"
            target="_blank"
            class="underline cursor-pointer">by joining the Discord Server</a
          >, or by sending an email to feedback@tandagames.com (you can include
          your name if you want to be publicly credited with helping develop the
          game). Thank you!
        </p>
        <p class="italic my-2">Updated July, 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <FeedbackEmigrationGame
      title="Playtester's Feedback"
      client:visible
      discordLink="https://discord.gg/aDV6NY73H2"
      version={VERSION}
      changelog={changelog}
    />
  </main>
</Layout>
